could use for Ch4 context about toxicity-efficacy relationship.\n\nP0319: 2026 review on microbiome-metabolites-tumor immunity. Strong for Ch3 (mechanisms), Ch5 (interventions), Ch6 (challenges).\n\nP0320: 2025 review on gut microbiota in breast cancer. Tumor-specific (Ch4), mechanisms (Ch3), interventions (Ch5).\n\nP0321: 2023 abstract on microbiome and ICI in GI tumors. Intervention categories (Ch5), but abstract-level only.\n\nP0322: 2022 review on gut microbiome, ICI and irAEs in NSCLC. Good for Ch2, Ch3, Ch4 (antibiotics), Ch5.\n\nP0323: 2025 review on multiomics in cancer immunology, includes microbiome as \"dark matter\". Conceptual framework (Ch6), mechanisms (Ch3).\n\nP0324: 2025 mini-review on GI tumor immune microenvironment and resistance. Includes FMT evidence (Ch5), but focuses on TIME mechanisms beyond microbiome (Ch3, Ch4).\n\nP0325: 2026 review on TCM mechanisms via microbiome and TME. Mechanisms (Ch3), interventions (Ch5), but preclinical focus.\n\nP0326: 2020 perspective on microbiome-derived metabolome as predictor. Metabolite focus (Ch3), clinical evidence with conflicting results (Ch2, Ch6).\n\nP0327: 2024 NSCLC study with negative results on microbiome predicting ICI response. Important for Ch6 (challenges, negative evidence), Ch2 (context about tumor type specificity).\n\nP0328: 2026 review on gut microbiome in triple-negative breast cancer. Tumor-specific (Ch4), mechanisms (Ch3), interventions (Ch5).\n\nP0329: 2026 abstract on designed bacterial therapeutic improving ICI response. Intervention (Ch5), predictive modeling (Ch6).\n\nP0330: 2026 review on digital immune twins and multi-omic biomarkers in NSCLC. Includes microbiome mechanisms (Ch3), but focuses on AI/digital twin concept (Ch6).\n\nP0331: 2024 abstract on antibiotic-induced loss of microbiome metabolic output and CAR-T response. Not ICI, but mechanistic parallels (Ch3 with caution), antibiotic context (Ch4).\n\nP0332: 2025 review on intratumoural microbes and cancer immunotherapy.